% gateway-authority: what the gateway checks before it writes a record, one check per click, then Cyberbird's create. For build 4,
% "The gateway holds the authority and the records." Task 4.6, step 1, item 4. The abstract concept first (stages 1 to 4), the
% instance last (stage 5).
% Canvas 16.5 x 5.8 cm (\useasboundingbox), the slide column at about 1:1; box text 9 pt, labels and notes 8 pt.
% Stages:
%   1 A request (a method on an object) enters the Gateway, a tall box, and meets gate 1, "who": an OIDC token, a client key, or
%     a supervisor's runtime credential. Gates 2 and 3, the store and the reconcile loop are ghosts.
%   2 Gate 2, "what": the method's declared permission (principal kind, scope, role).
%   3 Gate 3, "which": the workspace and the object.
%   4 The store, "conditional update by resource version", with the write arrow to it, and the reconcile loop back to the gateway:
%     desired against observed, leases, inventory sweep.
%   5 In action: the request reads "sandbox create cyberbird"; gate 1 "Rahul's client key" with the captured status line; gate 2
%     "CreateSandbox declares user, scope sandbox:write, role workspace user"; gate 3 "workspace default, object cyberbird"; the store holds
%     the record, resource version 14 at Ready; the loop compares the record with its container; a note on the supervisor's
%     own credential.
% Sources (all labels checked against the guide's chapter 5, commit be7af99):
%   Gate 1 (5.1): "Authentication verifies who is calling"; OIDC tokens and mutual TLS identify users; the authentication chain
%     in 5.1 and the supervisor's own credentials in 5.3 ("A supervisor does not reuse the user's OIDC token or client private
%     key. On Docker, Podman, and VM, its initial authentication is delivered through protected runtime material").
%   Gate 2 (5.2): "allowed principal kind, required scope, and role"; the table of roles there is Platform Admin, Workspace Admin,
%     Workspace User, and the last is the one with "Creating and using sandboxes". Passing the method check authorizes no object.
%   Gate 3 (5.2): "Handlers then check the selected workspace and object"; the CLI's --workspace defaults to "default"
%     (help-sandbox-create.txt, GLOBAL FLAGS).
%   Store (5.4): resource version, compare-and-swap; the first write of a new sandbox uses MustCreate (4.3).
%   Loop (5.5, 5.6): reconciliation compares durable records with backend resources; the inventory sweep runs every minute; a
%     renewable lease gives the reconciliation role to one replica.
% Captured lines in stage 5 (instructor-materials/hw2/feasibility): "Authentication: Authenticated (mTLS transport)" is a line of
% `openshell status` on Rahul's gateway (results.md, "Gateway check"); "Resource version: 14" is a line of
% `openshell sandbox get cyberbird` after the run, at Ready (cyberbird/sandbox-record.txt).
% Rulings against the brief's wording (recorded in the report): gate 2's "user, scope sandbox, role writer" becomes what the
%   gateway's own proto declares for rpc CreateSandbox at commit be7af99 (proto/openshell.proto line 48: auth_mode "bearer",
%   scope "sandbox:write", workspace_role "user"), so "user, scope sandbox:write, role workspace user", the guide's name for the
%   role that creates sandboxes (5.2); "record cyberbird, revision 1" becomes the captured "resource version 14 at Ready"
%   ("revision" in OpenShell names a policy revision, and nothing captured shows version 1). Text under 8 pt is avoided: the
%   captured status line is set in 8 pt typewriter.
% Colour: no magenta (no adversary). The gate being explained carries the style's hl outline; gates already reached keep their
% navy numbers; the ones not reached are dashed ghosts with their text in light grey. Nothing moves between stages: every box
% has a fixed size.
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm]
  \useasboundingbox (0,0) rectangle (16.5,5.8);
  \hyphenpenalty=10000 \exhyphenpenalty=10000 \frenchspacing
  \def\sAction{5}
  \tikzset{
    ghostbox/.style={draw=ibmfg!25, text=ibmfg!35, fill=white, dashed},
    ghflow/.style={-{Stealth[length=2.2mm]}, thick, draw=ibmfg!25, dashed},
    ghnum/.style={circle, draw=ibmfg!25, text=ibmfg!35, fill=white, dashed, inner sep=0pt, minimum size=4.6mm,
                  font=\sffamily\footnotesize\bfseries},
    gtext/.style={font=\sffamily\footnotesize, anchor=west, text width=5.65cm, inner sep=1pt, align=left},
    solid/.style={outer sep=0pt},
  }
  % \inst{text}: an instance line of stage 5, in navy
  \newcommand{\inst}[1]{\textcolor{deckNavy}{\bfseries #1}}
  % \link{style}{ghost style}{stage}{path}: an arrow, a ghost before its stage
  \newcommand{\link}[4]{\ifnum\stage<#3 \draw[#2] #4;\else \draw[#1] #4;\fi}
  % \gate{k}{y}{generic text}{in-action text}: the numbered circle and its text on the row at height y; a ghost before stage k,
  % outlined on stage k, plain after it; stage 5 prints the in-action text
  \newcommand{\gate}[4]{%
    \ifnum\stage<#1
      \node[ghnum, solid] (g#1) at (4.15,#2) {#1};
      \node[gtext, text=ibmfg!35] (t#1) at (4.5,#2) {#3};
    \else
      \node[evnum, solid] (g#1) at (4.15,#2) {#1};
      \ifnum\stage=\sAction
        \node[gtext] (t#1) at (4.5,#2) {#4};
      \else
        \node[gtext] (t#1) at (4.5,#2) {#3};
      \fi
    \fi
    \ifnum\stage=#1 \draw[hl] (3.75,#2-0.58) rectangle (10.3,#2+0.58);\fi}

  % heading
  \ifnum\stage<\sAction
    \node[lab, anchor=west, text=deckGrey] at (0.05,5.6) {a request to the gateway};
  \else
    \node[zonelab, anchor=west, inner sep=1pt] at (0.05,5.6) {in action: Cyberbird};
  \fi

  % the request, at the left, level with gate 1
  \ifnum\stage<\sAction
    \node[mnode, solid, minimum width=2.75cm, minimum height=1.2cm, text width=2.5cm] (req) at (1.425,4.1)
      {\textbf{request}\\a method on an object};
  \else
    \node[mnode, solid, minimum width=2.75cm, minimum height=1.2cm, text width=2.5cm] (req) at (1.425,4.1)
      {\textbf{request}\\\inst{sandbox create}\\\inst{cyberbird}};
  \fi

  % the gateway: a tall box with the three gates stacked inside
  \node[rnode, solid, minimum width=6.8cm, minimum height=5.0cm] (gw) at (7.0,2.8) {};
  \node[font=\sffamily\small\bfseries, anchor=north] at (7.0,5.22) {Gateway};

  \gate{1}{4.1}{\textbf{who:} OIDC token, client key, or a supervisor's runtime credential}
    {\textbf{who:} \inst{Rahul's client key}\\{\ttfamily\footnotesize\textcolor{deckGrey}{Authentication: Authenticated}}\\{\ttfamily\footnotesize\textcolor{deckGrey}{(mTLS transport)}}}
  \gate{2}{2.8}{\textbf{what:} the method's declared permission (principal kind, scope, role)}
    {\textbf{what:} \inst{CreateSandbox declares}\\\inst{user, scope sandbox:write,}\\\inst{role workspace user}}
  \gate{3}{1.5}{\textbf{which:} the workspace and the object}
    {\textbf{which:} \inst{workspace default,}\\\inst{object cyberbird}}

  % the store, at the right, level with gate 3
  \ifnum\stage<4
    \node[gnode, solid, ghostbox, minimum width=4.4cm, minimum height=1.75cm, text width=4.1cm] (store) at (14.25,1.5)
      {\textbf{store}\\conditional update\\by resource version};
  \else
    \ifnum\stage=\sAction
      \node[gnode, solid, minimum width=4.4cm, minimum height=1.75cm, text width=4.1cm] (store) at (14.25,1.5)
        {\textbf{store}\\record \inst{cyberbird}\\\inst{resource version 14}\\\inst{at Ready}};
    \else
      \node[gnode, solid, minimum width=4.4cm, minimum height=1.75cm, text width=4.1cm, hl] (store) at (14.25,1.5)
        {\textbf{store}\\conditional update\\by resource version};
    \fi
  \fi

  % arrows: the request in, down through the gates, the write out, the reconcile loop back
  \link{flow}{ghflow}{1}{(req.east) -- (g1.west)}
  \link{flow}{ghflow}{2}{(g1.south) -- (g2.north)}
  \link{flow}{ghflow}{3}{(g2.south) -- (g3.north)}
  \link{flow}{ghflow}{4}{(10.4,1.5) -- (store.west)}
  \ifnum\stage<4
    \draw[ghflow] (store.north) |- (10.4,3.6);
  \else
    \ifnum\stage=4
      \draw[back, draw=deckNavy, line width=1.6pt] (store.north) |- (10.4,3.6);
    \else
      \draw[back] (store.north) |- (10.4,3.6);
    \fi
  \fi
  \ifnum\stage<4
    \node[lab, anchor=south, text width=3.5cm, text=ibmfg!35] at (12.3,3.68)
      {reconcile: desired against observed, leases, inventory sweep};
  \else
    \ifnum\stage=\sAction
      \node[lab, anchor=south, text width=3.5cm] at (12.3,3.68)
        {reconcile: record \inst{cyberbird} against its container};
    \else
      \node[lab, anchor=south, text width=3.5cm] at (12.3,3.68)
        {reconcile: desired against observed, leases, inventory sweep};
    \fi
  \fi

  % in action: the supervisor's own credential (guide 5.3)
  \atstage{\sAction}{\node[font=\sffamily\footnotesize, anchor=north west, text width=3.2cm, inner sep=1pt, align=left]
    at (0.05,3.0) {\inst{Its supervisor}\\signs in with runtime material bound at creation, not this key};}
\end{tikzpicture}%
